values ('703ee2b2-cdc5-577a-8dc6-96a8fbbd2c1b', 'wg7-informative-writing-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g7-informative-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$How Hot Air Balloons Fly$q$, $q$(1) A hot air balloon can rise thousands of feet into the sky without an engine or wings. (2) The secret is a simple fact about air. (3) When air is heated, its tiny particles spread farther apart, so the air becomes less dense. (4) Density is the amount of matter packed into a certain amount of space. (5) Because the hot air inside the balloon is less dense than the cooler air outside, the balloon floats upward, much like a cork rises in water.

(6) A balloon has three main parts. (7) The envelope is the large fabric bag that holds the heated air. (8) Below it hangs the basket, which carries the pilot and passengers. (9) Between them sits the burner, a device that shoots a flame up into the envelope. (10) My neighbor has a red kite that she flies at the park on windy days.

(11) The pilot controls height by changing the temperature of the air inside the envelope. (12) A long blast from the burner heats the air and makes the balloon climb. (13) Opening a vent at the top lets hot air escape, so the balloon sinks. (14) The pilot cannot steer left or right, however. (15) Instead, the balloon drifts with the wind, which often blows in different directions at different heights.$q$, 'draft')
