   $q$Which sentence would make the best concluding statement for the report?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Glowworms and some deep sea fish can also make their own light.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Fireflies are a kind of beetle, not a kind of fly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Turning off porch lights is the only way to save fireflies.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"},{"text":"A firefly's cool, blinking light is a remarkable way to communicate, and darker nights may help keep that signal shining.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A firefly's cool, blinking light is a remarkable way to communicate, and darker nights may help keep that signal shining.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion connects the report's main ideas: how fireflies make light, why they flash, and the problem of bright lights. The porch light sentence is tempting but overstates the report, which names bright lights as one cause, not the only one.$q$, 'draft', '2594b992-b8aa-5968-a43c-5d7b263e0eff')
